course: dictionary
lesson: 8439
title: Sadly, and what it can mean
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Sadly» is an adverb. Adverbs tell us how something is done. Toad thinks a long time and then says sadly: «You have conquered, my friends...» Here sadly means in a sad way: Toad speaks in an unhappy voice.
explain: When sadly starts a sentence, it means unfortunately, or it is sad that... It is a gentle way to share bad news. Try the swap: «Unfortunately, we cannot come to the party» still makes sense, so this meaning fits.
explain: Sadly can also mean very much or badly, as in the phrase sadly mistaken. Someone who is sadly mistaken is badly wrong. The words around sadly are your clues, so read the whole sentence before you choose a meaning.
fact: Sadly is an adverb, so it tells us how, when or where something happens.
fact: «Sadly» can mean in a sad way, as in «says sadly».
fact: At the start of a sentence, «sadly» means unfortunately: it is sad that...
fact: «Sadly mistaken» means badly wrong. It does not mean unhappy.
fact: Some fronted adverbials show the speaker's opinion, like Frankly, Luckily and Sadly.
exercise: Toad thinks a long time and then says sadly: «You have conquered, my friends...» How does Toad speak? | In a hurry, running off | *In a sad, unhappy way | In a loud, cheerful shout | With his eyes closed and his hands in his pockets
exercise: «Sadly, we cannot come to the party.» What does sadly mean at the start of this sentence? | Very loudly | In a happy, joyful way | *Unfortunately, it is sad that we cannot come
exercise: «They jump about like mad things, then suddenly sit down sadly and quietly.» How do they sit down? | At night, under the stars | All of them together, in a line | Very far away | *In a sad way
test: «He was sadly mistaken about the weather.» What does sadly mean here? | In a sad, tearful way | Happily, with a smile | Quietly and slowly | *Badly: he was badly wrong
test: Which sentence uses sadly to give bad news gently? | «She sang sadly in the bath.» | «The bus was sadly big and yellow.» | «He ran to the bus stop sadly, sulking.» | *«Sadly, the bus has broken down.»
exam: In «Sadly, we cannot come to the party», what does sadly mean? | Quickly, at once | Very loudly | Happily, with a big smile | *Unfortunately, it is sad that we cannot come
